{"n":11,"level":"A1","title":"I am, you are, he is","pt":"O verbo to be","scene":"kitchen","tod":"day","cast":["Ben","Lucia","Mia"],"fic":{"scene":"kitchen","tod":"day","decor":[],"cast":[{"p":{"hs":"side","outfit":"shirt","top":"#e8473b","hair":"blond","skin":"light","arms":"wave"}},{"p":{"hs":"long","outfit":"dress","top":"#5cb85c","hair":"black","skin":"brown","arms":"point"}},{"p":{"hs":"pigtails","outfit":"dress","top":"#4a90d9","hair":"black","skin":"brown","arms":"out"}}]},"minutes":64,"slides":[{"t":"cover","min":1,"title":"I am, you are, he is","pt":"O verbo to be","level":"A1","n":11,"cast":["Ben","Lucia","Mia"]},{"t":"goals","min":1,"goal":"Usar am, is e are para dizer quem somos e como estamos.","canDo":["Conjugar to be no afirmativo","Usar as formas curtas I'm, you're, he's","Descrever pessoas com adjetivos simples"]},{"t":"warm","min":2,"q":"Como você está hoje? Use uma palavra.","pt":"Colete adjetivos: happy, tired, hungry...","chips":["I am happy.","You are late.","He is tired.","She is in the kitchen."]},{"t":"curious","min":1,"title":"Be: o verbo mais importante","text":"To be é o verbo mais usado do inglês e serve para ser E estar. Ele é irregular em todos os tempos: am, is, are, was, were, been. Quase todo diálogo começa com ele.","kind":"Você sabia?"},{"t":"scene","min":1,"text":"Na cozinha comunitária, Ben e Lucia preparam o almoço e falam de como cada um está.","line":"Hi, Lucia! You are early.","who":["Ben","Lucia","Mia"]},{"t":"article","min":2,"title":"Lunch at the street kitchen","text":"Every Friday the neighbors cook together in the street kitchen. Ben is the chef and Lucia is his helper. Today the soup is hot and the bread is warm. The kids are hungry and the cook is tired, but everyone is happy. Mia is busy with the salad. At twelve o'clock, the lunch is ready. \"We are a team!\" says Ben. Everybody sits at the long table and eats together. The kitchen is noisy, warm and full of laughter.","pt":"Sexta é dia de cozinha coletiva: todos t